ja'e lo mi cilre ku ko jungau e'o fo lo do krinu be tu'a zo zei

I'm proud of myself; that sounds better to me in lojban than the
corresponding English would have.  I think {krinu} is the right "why", but
I'm not sure.

Also, how difficult would it be in the parser to give {bu} precedence?  I
feel wrong claiming that both {.abu} and {xy} are letterals if they don't
behave the same way.  Just my two cents.

