> >        non-A-non-B-hepatitis
> >
> > Shouldn't the {.a}s be {.abu}s?
>
> Not currently; zei grabs single words.
>
> http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=Magic+Words
>
> > It seems to me that {na'e zei .a} refers to a logical connective
> > that is not "or".
>
> I'm inclined to agree, but the lujvo coiner gets to define the
> meaning.
>
> Regardless, {zei} is a really crappy way to do *anything*, so I'm
> not inclined to clarify how to do things with it very much.
>
> -Robin
